# Two survivors inside a spin hint, for the same reason as most of ring_poll's.
#
#     for _ in 0..=( attempt % 8 )
#     {
#       core::hint::spin_loop();
#     }
#     true
#
# The loop bound decides how many hint instructions execute and nothing else.
# The arm returns the constant `true` either way. `% 8` becoming `+ 8` or `/ 8`
# changes the iteration count and no observable value, so no assertion can
# separate them.
#
# This does *not* excuse `pause`'s return value, which is tested, at both
# polarities, in this crate's own suite. What survives is only the backoff
# shape, which is a performance property. Asserting it would mean asserting on a
# clock, the same trade `ring_bench` refuses, for the same reason.

ring_wait/src/lib.rs:113:29: replace % with + in pause
ring_wait/src/lib.rs:113:29: replace % with / in pause
